{#
  Editorial masthead: shared frame, included by the base layout rather than
  composed per page. Content comes from _data/site.js and _data/nav.js.

  Three-column rail (location, stacked lockup, booking status) with the nav
  justified beneath, then a sentinel and the collapsed sticky bar.

  The wordmark A carries the crossbar-less alt-glyph, scoped to that single
  character. Never word-level font-feature-settings: ss01 also carries D, E, H,
  J, O and R, which the lockup has retired. The isotype is alt="" because the
  adjacent text already names the link.

  Below 1120px the rail does not render at all and the sticky bar becomes the
  masthead: always present, compacting on scroll rather than appearing. The
  four nav items move into the ink menu pane at the foot of this file, and the
  location and booking lines move into that pane's foot. See masthead.css for
  why the collapsed bar was reused rather than a second mobile header built.

  ONE nav list per viewport is exposed to assistive tech: above 1120 the rail
  nav and the condensed bar nav, below it only the menu's. The hidden ones are
  display:none, so no width shows two copies of the same four destinations.
#}
{% from "components/icon.njk" import icon %}

<header class="cs-masthead">
  <div class="cs-masthead__rail">
    <p class="cs-masthead__label cs-masthead__location">{{ site.location }}</p>

    <a class="cs-wordmark cs-wordmark--stacked" href="/" aria-label="{{ site.name }}, home">
      <img class="cs-wordmark__icon" src="/brand/Circulation-Studio-icon.svg" alt="" width="117" height="117">
      <span class="cs-wordmark__name">Circul<span class="alt-soft">a</span>tion</span>
      <span class="cs-wordmark__studio">Studio</span>
    </a>

    <a class="cs-masthead__label cs-masthead__booking" href="{{ site.booking.url }}">
      {{ site.booking.label }}
    </a>
  </div>

  <nav class="cs-masthead__nav" aria-label="Primary">
    <ul class="cs-masthead__navlist">
      {% for item in nav.primary %}
        <li><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.label }}</a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </nav>
</header>

{# Watched by the observer in main.js. Once this leaves the viewport the
   masthead has scrolled away and the sticky bar reveals. #}
<div class="cs-masthead__sentinel" data-masthead-sentinel aria-hidden="true"></div>

<div class="cs-stickybar" data-sticky-masthead>
  <a class="cs-wordmark cs-wordmark--inline" href="/" aria-label="{{ site.name }}, home">
    <img class="cs-wordmark__icon" src="/brand/Circulation-Studio-icon.svg" alt="" width="117" height="117">
    <span class="cs-wordmark__name">Circul<span class="alt-soft">a</span>tion Studio</span>
  </a>

  <nav class="cs-stickybar__nav" aria-label="Primary, condensed">
    {% for item in nav.primary %}
      <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.label }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
  </nav>

  {# Mobile and tablet controls, hidden above 1120px where the nav above
     carries the same destinations inline. The booking note shows on the
     tablet only; on the phone it moves into the menu foot with the location,
     per the design. #}
  <div class="cs-stickybar__controls">
    <a class="cs-stickybar__booking" href="{{ site.booking.url }}">{{ site.booking.label }}</a>

    <button class="cs-stickybar__toggle" type="button"
            data-menu-toggle aria-controls="cs-menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu">
      {{ icon("menu", 24) }}
    </button>
  </div>
</div>

{# Mobile menu: full-pane ink overlay. Rendered at every width and hidden
   above 1120px in CSS, so there is one copy of it and no template branch.

   Open and close state, the focus trap and Escape live in main.js. The pane is
   hidden with visibility, not the hidden attribute, which keeps it out of the
   tab order while closed and still lets the fade run.

   ALT-GLYPH: the single A here, nothing else. Not the nav labels, not the
   location, not the booking note. The wordmark carries no icon on this pane,
   but that does NOT license the O device: DESIGN_SYSTEM.md permits the O only
   where the mark is absent AND the type is not the wordmark. The wordmark
   never carries a device on its O, in any lockup. #}
<div class="cs-menu" id="cs-menu" data-menu>
  <div class="cs-menu__bar">
    {# Inert on purpose, matching the design. The closed bar's lockup is the
       link home; a second one here would put a fifth destination in a
       four-item menu. #}
    <span class="cs-wordmark cs-wordmark--inline cs-wordmark--on-deep">
      <span class="cs-wordmark__name">Circul<span class="alt-soft">a</span>tion Studio</span>
    </span>

    <button class="cs-menu__dismiss" type="button" data-menu-close aria-label="Close menu">
      {{ icon("close", 24) }}
    </button>
  </div>

  <nav class="cs-menu__nav" aria-label="Primary">
    {% for item in nav.primary %}
      <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.label }}</a>
    {% endfor %}
  </nav>

  <div class="cs-menu__foot">
    <span class="cs-menu__location">{{ site.location }}</span>
    <a class="cs-menu__booking" href="{{ site.booking.url }}">{{ site.booking.label }}</a>
  </div>
</div>
